The case below gives the figures. In a profiling run over a buffer, an O(n) sweep over 669 keys costs around 6 machine actions apiece. What total should the profiler report?

The loop under study is:

```cpp
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 669; ++i) {
    total += 6;
}
```

What total is reported?

During a single array pass, an O(n) sweep over 916 samples costs some 2 steps for each. What is the expected operation count?

The loop under study is:

```cpp
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 916; ++i) {
    total += 2;
}
```

What total is reported?
